    "created_at": "2016-04-12T19:07:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-12T19:07:25Z",
    "body": "Hi @senolv,\n\nSee https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/FAQ#Is_there_a_process_for_adding_new_features_to_a_specification.3F. In general, a feature getting broad cross-browser interest requires it solving a new problem, not simply being nicer syntax for an old problem. So just adding methods like this is not likely to be interesting.\n\nBut! In this particular case, the story is a bit more interesting. There is a very related \"new problem\" we're interested in solving: how to give web workers, including service workers, access to cookies.\n\nOne way to do this would be a simple API like `self.cookie` in workers, which behaves the same as `document.cookie`. That might still be the way we go. But some enterprising folk, in particular @bsittler, have tried to do something more ambitious, and come up with a new cookie API that we could expose in workers. He's working on it over at https://github.com/bsittler/async-cookies-api. If that work goes well (there's a lot of tricky outstanding issues; see the issues list) then we could probably add it to both workers and windows, which would both satisfy your request for a nicer syntax, and solve the \"new problem\" of giving workers cookie access.\n",
